    "https://udayton.edu/careers/index.php": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers at UD : University of Dayton, Ohio Skip to content /////// Careers at UD Home Come Fly With Us Founded in 1850, the University of Dayton is a top-tier Catholic research university. Here, we adapt to meet the needs of the changing world. We turn big dreams into bold moves. And we build vibrant, inclusive and diverse communities that are marked by openness, cooperation, collegiality and a sense of service. Diverse experiences and backgrounds are vital to enriching our learning environment, advancing innovation, thinking critically and creatively, and solving complex problems. We're passionately striving to create a brighter tomorrow — together. View Staff and Faculty Jobs View Student Jobs Subscribe to Job Alerts Join Our Talent Network A Vibrant, Welcoming Community About UD UD is rooted in faith and dedicated to the common good. We invite people with diverse talents, interests and backgrounds to advance our common mission. Learn More About UD Explore the City of Dayton Add 423 Scenic Acres to Your Career Path Benefits Our competitive, flexible benefits help you achieve your goals and bring balance to your work — and the rest of your life. Explore Benefits Dual Career Resources We are pleased to provide support for spouses of prospective and newly hired faculty. While we cannot guarantee placement, we serve as an effective resource and support system for your spouse. Explore Dual Career Resources Disability Accommodation The University aims to increase access and inclusion for individuals with disabilities; reasonable accommodations may be provided upon request. Applicants can contact the Office of Human Resources at hr@udayton.edu or 937-229-2541 to obtain more information or request accommodation. Read the Accommodations Policy Nondiscrimination Policy The University of Dayton is committed to providing an educational and employment environment that is free from discrimination, and in compliance with federal and state laws. Read Nondiscrimination Policy Research for the Common Good UDRI The University of Dayton Research Institute is a globally recognized leader in research, development and transition of technologies that advance science and benefit the world. UDRI addresses the mission-critical needs of the Department of Defense and private industry while setting the standard for tomorrow's breakthroughs. Explore Careers at UDRI Contact Human Resources 300 College Park Dayton, Ohio                        45469 - 1649 937-229-2541 email Linkedin Campus Security and Fire Safety Report UD reports crime and fire statistics as required by federal law. The Annual Fire Safety and Security Report outlines reportable statistics and measures taken to protect the campus community, as well as institutional policies and programs related to safety and security. View Report Take the Next Step Apply for Jobs Subscribe to Job Alerts Join Our Talent Network Explore Majors and Programs Academic Calendar Careers Libraries News Next Steps Request Info Apply Visit Give Connect Facebook X Instagram Youtube Linkedin Directions Contact Us 300 College Park Dayton, Ohio 45469 937-229-1000 info@udayton.edu Porches Policies Safety Report a Concern Privacy Nondiscrimination Compliance"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/875/cw/en-us/listing/": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities : University of Dayton, Ohio",
      "description": "Employment Opportunities : University of Dayton, Ohio Home About Academics Admission Financial Aid Diversity Research Life at Dayton Athletics We Soar University Overview Catholic, Marianist Education Points of Pride Mission and Identity History Partnerships Location Faculty and Staff Directory Social Media Directory We Soar Academics Overview Program Listing Academic Calendar College of Arts and Sciences School of Business Administration School of Education and Health Sciences School of Engineering School of Law Professional and Continuing Education Intensive English Program University Libraries Admission Overview Undergraduate Transfer UD Sinclair Academy International Graduate Law Professional and Continuing Education Campus Visit Affordability Overview Undergraduate Transfer International Graduate Law Consumer Information Diversity Overview Office of Diversity and Inclusion Equity Compliance Office Research Overview Momentum: Our Research UD Research Institute Office for Research Technology Transfer Campus Overview Arts and Culture Campus Recreation City of Dayton Clubs and Organizations Housing and Dining Student Resources and Services Athletics Overview Dayton Flyers We Soar Overview Priorities Goals Impact Stories Volunteer Make a Gift Next Steps Apply Schedule a Visit Request Info Give Info For: Select Audience Alumni and Friends Current Students Future Students High School Counselors International Students Parents Faculty and Staff Select Audience Explore More News Academic Calendar Event Calendar Libraries Careers Employment Opportunities Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Department Open Date Close Date Senior Research Engineer – Defense Quantum Applications Lead Innovation & Collaboration Office - 250800 September 15, 2026 September 29, 2026 Turn Your Operational Experience into the Next Generation of Defense Capability.\n\nUDRI is looking for an experienced military leader and problem solver to help turn real-world defense challenges into the next generation of quantum and advanced computing applications.\n\nIf you've spent your career understanding military operations, making decisions under uncertainty, solving complex problems, and leading technical teams—and you're interested in what comes next—we want to talk to you. MBSE Systems Engineer Applied Digital Solutions - 250612 September 15, 2026 Open until filled Join the University of Dayton Research Institute (UDRI) as a Model-Based Systems Engineering (MBSE) Modeler where you will bring your MBSE expertise to transform data integration and software lifecycles into powerful system models! Located in the vibrant tech hub of Dayton, Ohio, you'll contribute to cutting-edge research that directly impacts national security and technological advancement. UDRI offers an exceptional work environment where research excellence thrives. You'll enjoy comprehensive benefits including robust health coverage, retirement contributions, and professional development opportunities. Apply today! Accounts Payable Manager General Ledger - 250212 September 15, 2026 Open until filled Join UDRI by leading Accounts Payable today while building the scalable processes, strong controls, and high-performing team needed for tomorrow. Qualified candidates are encouraged to apply and take the next step in a rewarding leadership opportunity as an Accounts Payable Manager! Logistics Program Integrator Associate Sustainment Product Supp - 250721 September 15, 2026 September 29, 2026 Are you interested in working for UDRI, a national leader in scientific and engineering research, serving government, industry and nonprofit customers? UDRI contributes to the fulfillment of the University’s commitments to education, research and public service through the involvement of students, faculty, Staff, and external partners. Established as the research arm of the University of Dayton in 1956, UDRI achieved $2.75 billion in cumulative sponsored research in 2020. We invite qualified candidates to apply for our AM Engineer opening! This full time and benefit eligible position offers health, dental and vision insurance, retirement, disability, tuition assistance for you and your dependents, vacation, sick, and holiday pay. Apply today! CNC Programmer Adv Mfg Dayton - 250712 September 15, 2026 Open until filled UDRI invites qualified candidates to apply for our CNC Programmer opening! This position is located at the Advanced Technology and Training Center (ATTC) – Dayton, OH at the University of Dayton Research Institute. The CNC Programmer will provide support and technical expertise for the design, manufacture, and post processing of critical sustainment components for the USAF and commercial customers. Technology Transition Analyst - NDI SME Applied Sustainment Technologies - 250741 September 15, 2026 Open until filled The University of Dayton Research Institute (UDRI) invites qualified applicants to apply for our Technology Transition Analyst - NDI SME for a technology transition analyst role. This position will be located at Tinker AFB, OK. Apply today! Senior System Engineer or Lead System Engineer Entpr Enabling Solutions - 804600 September 15, 2026 Open until filled Join the University of Dayton's IT department and play a key role in supporting the reliable, secure technology services that power our University community.  In this role you will work alongside other members of the Enterprise Enabling Technologies team to maintain our server environments, monitor system performance and security, apply upgrades, and help support a stable infrastructure. You will also work with other cross-functional teams across UDit to build new enterprise systems. This is a full-time, benefit-eligible position offering a comprehensive benefits package, including health, dental, retirement, paid time off, holidays and tuition assistance. Apply today! Systems Engineer or Senior Systems Engineer Entpr Enabling Solutions - 804600 September 15, 2026 Open until filled Join the University of Dayton's IT department and play a key role in supporting the reliable, secure technology services that power our University community.  In this role you will work alongside other members of the Enterprise Enabling Technologies team to maintain our server environments, monitor system performance and security, apply upgrades, and help support a stable infrastructure. You will also work with other cross-functional teams across UDit to build new enterprise systems. This is a full-time, benefit-eligible position offering a comprehensive benefits package, including health, dental, retirement, paid time off, holidays and tuition assistance. Apply today! Master Sustainment Technician - CNC Programmer Adv Mfg MG - 250713 September 15, 2026 September 29, 2026 Are you interested in working for UDRI, a national leader in scientific and engineering research, serving government, industry and nonprofit customers? UDRI contributes to the fulfillment of the University’s commitments to education, research and public service through the involvement of students, faculty, Staff, and external partners. Established as the research arm of the University of Dayton in 1956, UDRI achieved $2.75 billion in cumulative sponsored research in 2020. We invite qualified candidates to apply for our AM Engineer opening! This full time and benefit eligible position offers health, dental and vision insurance, retirement, disability, tuition assistance for you and your dependents, vacation, sick, and holiday pay. Apply today! Associate Research IT Professional Help Desk - 250223 September 11, 2026 Open until filled Build. Support. Troubleshoot. Grow. — Join UDRI's IT Team! The Associate IT Research Professional provides support to a growing business and emerging IT infrastructure. Apply today! Nutrition Assistant SEHS Bombeck Family Learning Cntr - 210300 September 08, 2026 Open until filled Join our team as a Nutrition Assistant and help provide healthy meals that fuel children's growth, learning, and success every day! We invite qualified applicants to apply for our Nutrition Assistant opening within the Bombeck Center. This is a full time benefit eligible position that offers health, dental and vision insurance, retirement, disability, tuition assistance for you and your dependents, vacation/sick accrual and holiday pay. Apply today! Assistant Director, Fraternity and Sorority Life Fraternity & Sorority Life - 700210 September 08, 2026 Open until filled Ready to shape the future of a vibrant fraternity and sorority community?  We're seeking a forward-thinking, collaborative, student-centered professional to join the University of Dayton as our next Assistant Director of Fraternity and Sorority Life.  Here, you could design transformative leadership initiatives, coach FSL councils and chapters, and serve as a vital collaborator in community-wide safety and risk management. Apply today! Cook's Helper Dining Serv - VWK - 800611 September 08, 2026 Open until filled Join the team behind great campus dining experiences! We’re looking for dependable, motivated individuals who enjoy working in a fast-paced kitchen environment and take pride in preparing quality food and providing outstanding customer service. From assisting with food preparation and maintaining a clean, safe kitchen to serving guests with a friendly attitude and processing orders efficiently, every role plays an important part in creating a positive dining experience for our campus community. Apply to our Cook's Helper opening today! Salad Maker Dining Serv - Central Production - 800621 September 08, 2026 Open until filled Join the Dining Services team as a Salad Maker at the University of Dayton and be part of a workplace that values its employees and the campus community. Prepare fresh salads, grab-and-go favorites, and other quality food items while following recipes and production guidelines and maintaining a clean, safe workspace. Enjoy the opportunity to grow with the University while taking advantage of excellent employee benefits and being part of a team that makes a difference every day. Production Supervisor Dining Serv - VWK - 800611 September 08, 2026 Open until filled Bring your leadership skills to Dining Services at the University of Dayton! As a working supervisor, you’ll be hands-on with food production while guiding and supporting a diverse team of BU, part-time, and student employees. Help create quality food, keep operations running efficiently, and make a difference in the campus dining experience. Join a team that values its employees and offers excellent benefits and opportunities to grow with the University. Apply to our Production Supervisor opening today! Cook Dining Serv - Marycrest - 800612 September 08, 2026 Open until filled Serve. Connect. Grow. Build Your Future at the University of Dayton. Great work environment. Great benefits. Tuition assistance for you and eligible family members. Join our Dining Team and enjoy the opportunity to build your career while investing in your future.\n\nAs a Cook, you’ll prepare high-quality food by following recipes and established standards, help maintain a clean and organized kitchen, and work with the team to develop and create new recipes and menu ideas. Your skills and creativity will help provide a great dining experience for our students, faculty, staff, and guests. Apply today! Part-Time Catering Services Attendant II Dining Serv - Catering - 800618 September 03, 2026 Open until filled We are looking for individuals with diverse talents and backgrounds to join our nationally recognized team that is committed to providing exciting and healthy food options to students, faculty and staff on campus. We offer excellent benefits including paid leave and tuition assistance. The University of Dayton is proud to be named the Best Place to Work in the annual Best of Dayton contest. Part-Time Catering Services Attendant I Dining Serv - Catering - 800618 September 03, 2026 Open until filled We are looking for individuals with diverse talents and backgrounds to join our nationally recognized team that is committed to providing exciting and healthy food options to students, faculty and staff on campus. We offer excellent benefits including paid leave and tuition assistance. The University of Dayton is proud to be named the Best Place to Work in the annual Best of Dayton contest. AM Design Engineer Adv Mfg Engineering - 250714 September 03, 2026 September 17, 2026 Are you interested in working for UDRI, a national leader in scientific and engineering research, serving government, industry and nonprofit customers? UDRI contributes to the fulfillment of the University’s commitments to education, research and public service through the involvement of students, faculty, Staff, and external partners. Established as the research arm of the University of Dayton in 1956, UDRI achieved $2.75 billion in cumulative sponsored research in 2020. We invite qualified candidates to apply for our AM Engineer opening! This full time and benefit eligible position offers health, dental and vision insurance, retirement, disability, tuition assistance for you and your dependents, vacation, sick, and holiday pay. Apply today! Assistant Professor of Practice or Lecturer specializing in Construction Engineering and Management SoE Exper Learning & Stdnt Success - 220100 September 02, 2026 October 18, 2026 Calling all Construction Engineering and Management Professionals:\n\nAre you interested in bringing your practical knowledge and experience in Construction Engineering and Management to educating the next generation of professionals?  Are you interested in developing unique practices and new experiential learning strategies? Are you looking for a university that educates the whole person and integrates learning and scholarship with leadership and service?\n\t\nIf so, the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering and Engineering Mechanics at the University of Dayton, located in Dayton, OH invites you to apply for a faculty position as an Assistant Professor of Practice or Lecturer specializing in Construction Engineering and Management to begin January 2027. More Jobs 71 Current Opportunities To view the position details and/or apply to an open position, click on the position title. All positions close at 11:55 pm EST, unless otherwise noted on the posting. To learn more about our benefits, please click here. Position Department Open Date Close Date Senior Research Engineer – Defense Quantum Applications Lead Innovation & Collaboration Office - 250800 September 15, 2026 September 29, 2026 Turn Your Operational Experience into the Next Generation of Defense Capability.\n\nUDRI is looking for an experienced military leader and problem solver to help turn real-world defense challenges into the next generation of quantum and advanced computing applications.\n\nIf you've spent your career understanding military operations, making decisions under uncertainty, solving complex problems, and leading technical teams—and you're interested in what comes next—we want to talk to you. MBSE Systems Engineer Applied Digital Solutions - 250612 September 15, 2026 Open until filled Join the University of Dayton Research Institute (UDRI) as a Model-Based Systems Engineering (MBSE) Modeler where you will bring your MBSE expertise to transform data integration and software lifecycles into powerful system models! Located in the vibrant tech hub of Dayton, Ohio, you'll contribute to cutting-edge research that directly impacts national security and technological advancement. UDRI offers an exceptional work environment where